I think I have a solution.
I am going to use a stack to keep track of the nodes.
I will start with the first node and push it into the stack.
Then I will iterate through the nodes and if the node is not in the stack, I will push it into the stack.
If the node is in the stack, I will pop it out and push the next node into the stack.
I will keep doing this until the stack is empty.
Here is the code:
public static void main(String[] args) {
    String[] nodes = { "qgv", "qxc", "qgv", "qxc" };
    Stack<String> stack = new Stack<String>();
    stack.push(nodes[0]);
    for (int i = 1; i < nodes.length; i++) {
        if (!stack.contains(nodes[i])) {
            stack.push(nodes[i]);
        } else {
            String popped = stack.pop();
            stack.push(nodes[i]);
        }
    }
    while (!stack.isEmpty()) {
        String popped = stack.pop();
        System.out.println(popped);
    }
}

